Ah that was fun. I'm bored with the rogue at the moment (she sprinted
down to Medusa with no particular effort but needs some gear before
proceeding), so I started a lawful human healer with the intent of
getting into Minetown at first level XP with some money. I took Kitty
into the dungeon as quickly as I could find stairs down. The 5th level
staircase was to a regular level, so I backed up and found the stair
to the mines on the 4th level. Up to this point the play was nothing
remarkable. Kitty had my back, and my front, and my sides, and was a
large cat well before entering the mines. I hadn't killed a monster
and I think I only hit one once by accident.

The gnomes not being my friends, things became more interesting in the
mines. The first mine level was lit and moderately open. We appeared
in the northwest corner and the Gs and hs began closing in from east
and south. Kitty took off to the east toward a large group of them
while I backed up into a nook and started writing Elbereth waiting for
him to return. Only he was out of sight making noises for a long
time ....

Meanwhile a group of 8-10 critters, mostly gnomes, collected around
me. I realized that waiting in a corner would have been fine if there
were 2-3 of them, but now there was nowhere for them to flee, so they
collected shoulder-to-shoulder in a pack around me 2-3 deep. Darts and
arrows and bolts began to fly. Every so often the Elbereth would break
down. Every so often I'd get hit by two or three missiles and quaff an
appropriate healing potion. It seemed unlikely I'd actually survive
this, because Kitty was gone a really looooong time, but slowly the
size of the group decreased as gnomes shot one another in the back in
their enthusiasm to shoot me. Eventually there was somewhere for them
to flee, in part because a dwarf was busy mining the adjacent dungeon,
and I scooted carefully from Elbereth to Elbereth until I found an
opening south. A single G followed me, but two gnome Zs appeared from
nowhere and joined chase. I found a much larger area and got against
the wall to continue to wait it out. Shortly, most of the darts and
arrows were at my feet so it had become a much lower stress
experience. When the noises elsewhere died down, I assumed Kitty had
done his work, and I started moving back to the north to meet up with
him. It was indeed a much quieter dungeon littered with sizable piles
of armor and weapons. We made it to the down staircase
uneventfully ....

The next level wasn't particularly notable because it was tighter and
the next down staircase was very close by.

The following down staircase (to the 3rd level) took us to more
caverns, but it shortly emerged that this was the funky Grotto
Minetown. Carefully and somewhat uneventfully I pushed Kitty along
ahead of me. At some point a gnome just out of sight ahead of me
zapped a hole in the ground and fell into it, and I followed right
behind. Whoops. Now I was down below Minetown and Kitty was nowhere to
be found. Not good. Really. Once again I drew a cluster of little
humanoids, but the space was more conducive to Elbereth hopping ... a
good thing because my pet was now upstairs wondering why I had stepped
into a hole. I worked my way free remarkably quickly and headed away
looking for the stairs back up. They weren't anywhere out in the open,
and I had to keep moving to stay ahead of the crowd behind me, so
there was no warning when I turned into a troll and then almost
immediately teleported (or was it the other way round?). Well, okay,
being polymorphed into a troll, that could be a lot worse, although
that robe I was kind of excited about was gone. I sprinted toward the
corner where the stairs had to be, and then hit another trap and
polyed into a black light. Aaaaaggh. The crowd caught up to me and I
was hit ... I hit back and, wham, I was human again, in the middle of
a bunch of monsters swinging in all directions and maiming one
another. I sneaked away from the stragglers under the cover of more
Elbereths (I must have written 50 or 100 of them so far) to the
stairs.

>From there, it was straightforward. I arrived at the temple at 1st
level with about 20hp (from quaffing most of my potions) and about
$2500.

Well, it was kind of straightforward, because I had run out of food,
and had to wait twice till I was fainting before praying for help.
Annoyingly, the deli was empty. I think it must have been full of
tripe rations before Kitty looted it. I had to get completely out of
the mines before I could find food.

I was down to 2-3 hit points several times, had 2-3 necessary prayers
(one for HP and two for food), was one successful Elbereth away from
death several times, and so on, but things never seemed completely out
of control. I probably hadn't killed a monster before getting to the
temple and with my Basic scalpel at Level 1 it didn't seem worth
trying.

So now I'm back at the top of the dungeon getting ready to work my way
down it properly, eating wall meat at my own pace.

Kind of entertaining.



